*** a lone ion ***
[Na+].C: salt
[Rb+].C: salt
[Ca+2].C: salt
[Zn+2].C: salt
[Al+3].C: salt
[Cr+3].C: salt
[Ru+4].C: salt
[Sn+4].C: salt
[Cl-].C: salt
[F-].C: salt
[S-2].C: salt
[Se-2].C: salt
*** a small inorganic molecule ***
S=[Fe].C: salt
Cl[Ag]: salt
S=[Sn]=S.C: salt
O=[Mn]=O.C: salt
Cl[Fe](Cl)Cl.C: salt
OCl(=O)=O.C: salt
OS(=O)(=O)O.C: salt
OP(=O)(O)O.C: salt
*** an inorganic ion of several atoms ***
[OH-].C: salt
[O-]Cl.C: salt
[O-]I=O.C: salt
[O-]N(=O).C: salt
[N+](=O)([O-])[O-].C: salt
O[Se](=O)[O-].C: salt
OP(=O)(O)[O-].C: salt
OS(=O)(=O)[O-].C: salt
*** several ions ***
[Na+].[Cl-].C: salt
[O-]S(=O)(=O)[O-].[K+].[K+].C: salt
*** no salt: nothing but organic molecules ***
c1ccccc1: no salt
C1=CC=C2C=CC=CC2=C1: no salt
*** no salt: the metal or the acid group is bonded ***
CC[Pb](CC)(CC)CC: no salt
C[Al](C)C: no salt
C1=CC=C(C=C1)[N+](=O)[O-]: no salt
C(C(=O)O)S(=O)(=O)O: no salt
*** stripSalt ***
CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC[N+]1C=CC=CC=1 -> 'CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC[N+]1=CC=CC=C1'
CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC[N+]1C=CC=CC=1.[Cl-] -> 'CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC[N+]1=CC=CC=C1'
CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC[N+]1C=CC=CC=1.O.O.O.O.O.O.O.O.O.O.[Cl-].[Cl-] -> 'CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC[N+]1=CC=CC=C1'
CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC[N+]1C=CC=CC=1.CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC[N+]1C=CC=CC=1.[O-]S(=O)(=O)[O-] -> 'CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC[N+]1=CC=CC=C1.CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC[N+]1=CC=CC=C1'
C(C(C(C(C(C(=O)O)O)O)O)O)O.C(C(C(C(C(C(=O)O)O)O)O)O)O.[Fe] -> 'C(O)C(O)C(O)C(O)C(O)C(O)=O.C(O)C(O)C(O)C(O)C(O)C(O)=O.[Fe]'
[NH4+].[O-]P(=O)([O-])[O-].[Fe+2] -> ''
*** the ion goes, not the atom whose place it has in the numbering ***
C1.[Na+].C1 -> 'CC'
*** a copy is stripped unless the molecule itself is asked for ***
the copy: CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC[N+]1=CC=CC=C1
the molecule after it: CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC[N+]1=CC=CC=C1.[Cl-]
stripped in place: CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC[N+]1=CC=CC=C1
*** a haptic complex is not a salt ***
ferrocene: atoms C C C C C C C C C C Fe, 2 haptic bonds, no salt
stripped: atoms C C C C C C C C C C Fe, 2 haptic bonds, no salt
*** its counter ion is ***
ferrocene and a chloride: atoms C C C C C C C C C C Cl Fe, 2 haptic bonds, salt
stripped: atoms C C C C C C C C C C Fe, 2 haptic bonds, no salt
*** a counter ion drawn between the atoms of the complex ***
stripped: atoms C C C C C C C C C C Fe, 2 haptic bonds, no salt
stripped in place: atoms C C C C C C C C C C Fe, 2 haptic bonds, no salt
*** a metal with inorganic ligands, held by a haptic bond ***
Zeise's salt: atoms C C Cl Cl Cl K Pt, 1 haptic bonds, salt
stripped: atoms C C Cl Cl Cl Pt, 1 haptic bonds, no salt
